WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:17.180
[Music]

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.609
[A solider wearing an apron puts on a facemask.]

00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:21.960
[Narrator:] You may not believe it, but this is really Private McGillicuddy!

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:22.830
[Washes hands and prepares an alcohol solution.]

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.830
[Narrator:] And his unusual activity is quite a surprise.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:31.910
Facemask, rubber gloves, disinfectant. Looks like he's preparing for an important operation.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.940
And he is! He is going to wash his mess gear.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:41.760
Although he's knocking himself out with all
this surgical etiquette, there's good reason for it.

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:45.820
Mac is not taking any more chances.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.370
So draw up a foxhole and we'll tell you why.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:52.600
Once upon a time, McGillicuddy ignored the
commandment:

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.660
[Sign tacked to tree reads Fifth Commandment: Mess Gear] 

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.100
[Narrator reading sign:] Thou shalt carefully and faithfully wash thy mess gear both before and after meals.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:07.570
For verily if thou become negligent in this
habit, thy guts shall be like knots in a wet rope.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.960
[Narrator:] So, while the other men went through their usual routine 

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.020
of cleaning their mess gear in scalding, hot soapy water,

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.500
McGillicuddy would stash his lazy butt under a coconut tree and wash his gear in his own way.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.820
[McGillicuddy licks his mess gear, puts dirt or sand inside it, shakes it around, 

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:31.780
wipes the gear with his shirt, and his mess gear shines.]

00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:36.630
[Narrator:] Sure, it looks clean - but it isn't!

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.730
You can't clean your mess gear by lickin'
it!

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.840
[McGillicuddy:] You can't?

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:47.480
[Narrator:] Naw, that just makes it look pretty! Here, look at it through this magnifying glass.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.560
[Magnifying glass appears above mess gear and spots of food are seen for the first time.]

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:53.870
[Narrator:] You see those little spots? They're bits of decayed food.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.420
No telling how long they've been there!

00:01:56.429 --> 00:01:57.299
Now watch closely.

00:01:57.299 --> 00:01:59.399
[Zoom-in on decayed food. A lizard-like germ crawls out of food.]

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.240
[Narrator:] Cute ain't he? That is a germ!

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:06.600
You ain't seen nothing yet. Take another gander.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.080
[McGillicuddy looks back at germ.]

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.569
[Narrator:] Now watch him multiply.

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:10.429
[Germs continue to split into other identical
germs.]

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.340
[Narrator:] 2! 4! 8! 16! 32! 64! 128! 256...

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.880
[Narrator becomes inaudible as he continues to count even faster and then skips to final number.]

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.640
[Narrator:] 8,970,562!

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:26.190
If you haven't been washing your mess gear properly, you've been eating those dirty microscopic scavengers!

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.000
[McGillicuddy looks sick and quickly runs to wash his mess gear in multiple tubs of scalding hot soapy water.]

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.280
[He finishes with a sigh of relief.]

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.860
[Narrator:] Well, that's more like it!

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:44.420
And that isn't all. You gotta wash it again
before you eat.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:49.879
Otherwise stray insects, like this fly for
instance, will foul it up again!

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.140
Maybe he's just been to the privy, maybe a garbage dump,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.000
and undoubtedly is packed with dysentery germs.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.540
[A fly with dirty dripping feet lands on mess
gear and skates around, leaving behind a trail of dirt.]

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.700
[Narrator:] If you're not careful, McGillicuddy, you will be too!

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.100
[McGillicuddy Is napping and is oblivious to the fly.]

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.920
[Narrator:] What's more...hey, ya knucklehead, wake up! I'm talkin' to ya!

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:09.510
There's a fly on your mess gear!

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.220
[McGillicuddy wakes up, swats the fly away, and looks proud of himself.]

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:16.100
[Narrator:] Now don't forget to wash that thing before ya eat.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:22.780
[Bugel sounds as Mac runs off with his mess gear.]

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:31.660
[McGillicuddy runs past soldiers washing mess gear, knocks over the bugel player, and is first in line for food.]

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.760
[Narrator:] That's right, Mac. First in line, last in brains.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.340
Let him pile all that good wholesome food
on top of those germs.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:48.360
[McGillicuddy stumbles out of mess tent, begins contorting himself and placing his hand over his stomach. He passes gas.]

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.740
[X-ray view of guts; narrator's voice booms
as guts are tied into knots.]

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:57.040
[Narrator:] Remember, Mac: "Thy guts shall be like knots in a wet rope!"

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.480
[McGillicuddy imagines himself in bed.]

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.200
[He imagines a large monster-like doctor towering over him,

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.060
about to cut into his stomach with a large knife.]

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:11.800
[Then sees a sinister-looking doctor plunging his face with a toilet plunger.]

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.920
[Next, two surgeons saw him in half
with a saw.]

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:19.640
[McGillicuddy imagines looking upwards and seeing a ring of grinning, snickering doctors.]

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.100
[Then he sees himself being forced to drink a giant bottle of castor oil...]

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.440
[imagines himself being held down with his
bottom facing a doctor...]

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:29.560
[who holds a hose connected to a tank that
says Capacity 50 Gal.]

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:34.360
[The tank empties into the hose and the soldier screams in pain.]

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.880
[McGillicuddy is then seen scrubbing his mess gear vigorously.]

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.760
[Narrator:] And so, kiddies, that is the story of Private McGillicuddy and the bad little germs,

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:47.040
and how he learned to wash his mess gear and live happily ever after.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:54.760
[Music]

